# WireMesh relay configuration (systemd EnvironmentFile).
# The relay is argv-configured: <bind-addr> <cert-dir> --controller <sync-host:port>
#
# The cert dir is the relay's DEDICATED state dir /var/lib/wiremesh-relay,
# created and owned (wiremesh:wiremesh, 0700) by the unit's StateDirectory=
# and by the package postinstall. Do NOT point it at /var/lib/wiremesh — that
# is the gateway/controller state dir (root-only 0700 when a gateway shares
# the host), and the User=wiremesh relay cannot read an identity enrolled
# there (ops finding 2026-07-27/28, "Relay Finding A"). The identity
# (ca.pem / relay.pem / relay.key — EACH file mode 0600, owned by the
# wiremesh service user) must be enrolled into the cert dir before first
# start: see `wiremesh-relay-enroll` and docs/install.md.
RELAY_ARGS=0.0.0.0:4443 /var/lib/wiremesh-relay --controller CONTROLLER_HOST:9500
